# Shell scripts keep LF endings, in the repository and in every working copy.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on Windows — rewrites checked-out text files
# to CRLF. For a shell script that is fatal rather than cosmetic: the kernel reads
# `#!/bin/sh\r` as an interpreter path that does not exist, and every command
# acquires a trailing CR. `install.sh` is documented as
# `curl -fsSL .../install.sh | sh`, where the pipe serves the LF blob regardless,
# but a clone-then-run on Windows would fail without this line.
*.sh text eol=lf
